LiquidLaneExecutor signed swap post actions
├── owner policy
│   ├── only the owner can replace a token's allowed leaves
│   ├── indexed getters and length expose replacements and clearing
│   ├── no allowed leaves prohibits post actions
│   ├── nonempty allowed leaves requires at least one post action
│   └── callbacks cannot replace the policy during funding or redemption
├── action authorization
│   ├── every supplied leaf must be allowed for the swapped RWA
│   ├── replaced and cross-token leaves remain forbidden despite root membership and roles
│   ├── masks use canonical leaf hashing and malformed masks revert
│   ├── adapter manages enforce proofs, Executor roles, and leaf budgets
│   └── subsets and repeated allowed leaves remain valid
├── redemption balance
│   ├── bare redemption preserves prior RWA holdings
│   ├── approval plus redemption may return the funding asset synchronously
│   ├── approval plus repeated redemption calls may consume the total in parts
│   ├── consumption equals swapped RWA amountIn rather than funding amountOut
│   └── underconsumption, overconsumption, approval-only, and increases revert
└── atomicity
    ├── failures roll back source withdrawal, swap, approvals, budgets, and redemption
    ├── later post failures roll back earlier redemptions
    └── redemption cannot reenter the Executor
